abstract: >-
  Analysis code and accepted manuscript source for a cross-sectional study of generative
  artificial intelligence (GenAI) task use among 1,105 respondents (659 students and 446
  teachers) at five Beijing universities. The study estimates a concave (inverted-U)
  association between GenAI task use frequency and perceived role-specific capability,
  shows that AI literacy shifts the location of the model-implied maximum, and finds that
  AI dependence follows a largely additive path driven by use, habit, and trust rather
  than by an inverted U. The package contains the scoring rules, the 33 lavaan CFA model
  specifications, the hierarchical regression, inverted-U test and bootstrap routines, the
  sensitivity analyses, and the nested cross-validation prediction and held-out TreeSHAP
  workflow, together with an output manifest linking every exported file to its location
  in the manuscript. Participant-level responses are not distributed.
keywords:
  - generative artificial intelligence
  - sustainable higher education
  - SDG 4
  - AI literacy
  - perceived learning agency
  - teaching innovation competence
  - AI dependence
  - cognitive offloading
  - inverted U relationship
